.\" Historical-source decision: The V1/V6/V7 as pages describe PDP-11 syntax and objects, not this Merlin-hosting command.
.\" Rendered by make man-pages; staged on play image in /usr/man/.
.TH AS 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
as \- run the legacy Merlin assembler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B as
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-o " object" ]
.I source
.SH DESCRIPTION
Assemble a Merlin-format source file using the legacy Merlin/Sweet16
core hosted as a maux process.
The -l option enables a listing; -o names the object output.
Source directives determine flat or relocatable output.
.PP
This command is retained for compatibility and independent comparison.
It is not an alias for nas(1).
The production native rebuild uses nas + ld + make.
.PP
The command is supplied on assembler development images, not on the
ordinary interactive play image.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/AS  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
nas(1), ld(1), nm(1), make(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 for an assembly with no errors, 1 for an assembly/runtime failure, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
Source and object storage are bounded by the legacy core's process-bank layout. Consult nas(1) for the production route rather than assuming a host Unix as interface.
